# PHP conventions

- Prefix every function `antiques_marketplace_`.
- Guard files with `if (!defined('ABSPATH')) { exit; }`.
- Comments and identifiers in English.
- Names must describe business intent (`convert_display_to_eur`, not `process`).
- Guard clauses and early returns; no nested `if` pyramids.
- Escape output: `esc_html`, `esc_url`, `esc_attr`. Prepare SQL with `$wpdb->prepare`.
- Cache expensive remote catalog work in transients. Do not call Google Translate on listing grids.
- Do not add Composer packages unless existing theme code already needs them.
- Keep business rules (FX, taxonomy, dashboard equations) out of templates; templates only render.
